/*
 * LARGE-SIGNAL, PARAMETRIC descent certificate for the pH bridge.
 *
 * theorem_ph_bridge.kyx proves the nonlinear sublevel invariance only at the
 * FIXED instance d=|D2|=3/10. The parametric companions theorem_ph_complete /
 * det_factorization / theorem_levelC_* are all evaluated at c=cos(delta)=1,
 * i.e. LINEARIZED at the equilibrium. This file is the missing quadrant:
 * V-dot <= 0 on the FULL large-signal domain c in [4/5,1], for ALL d in a
 * band, with d a SYMBOLIC parameter -- no linearization, no fixed instance.
 *
 * System (D1=K=1, machine 2 negative damping D2=-d, d>0):
 *   w1'=-w1-s,  w2'=d*w2+s,  s'=c(w1-w2),  c'=-s(w1-w2),  s^2+c^2=1.
 * pH-structured V (same closed form in d as the bridge):
 *   h=(1+4d)/6, a1=1+d, a2=(1+3d)/2,
 *   V = w1^2+w2^2+2(1-c)+h*s^2+a1*w1*s+a2*w2*s.
 *
 * KEY STRUCTURE: V' = x'M(c)x, x=(w1,w2,s), with M(c) AFFINE in c. Hence on
 * c in [4/5,1], x'M(c)x = (1-lambda) x'M(4/5)x + lambda x'M(1)x, lambda=5c-4 in
 * [0,1]: a CONVEX COMBINATION of the two endpoints. So
 *
 *   V' <= 0 on all of c in [4/5,1]   <==>   x'M(4/5)x <= 0  AND  x'M(1)x <= 0.
 *
 * This file proves BOTH endpoint quadratic forms are negative semidefinite for
 * ALL d in (0, 2/5], by QE (pure universal, 4 variables). Affine interpolation
 * (the one-line convex-combination identity above) then gives V'<=0 on the
 * entire large-signal domain c in [4/5,1] -- parametric in d.
 *
 * The two endpoint forms (cleared of positive denominators 6 and 30):
 *   6  * V'|_{c=1}   = N1(d,w1,w2,s)
 *   30 * V'|_{c=4/5} = N2(d,w1,w2,s)
 *
 * BAND: d in (0, 2/5] = 40% of the Routh boundary (d<1). The exact cap of this
 * fixed closed-form certificate on c>=4/5 is d~0.441 (N2 loses NSD there); 2/5
 * sits safely inside. This is NOT the tight pH cap (joint optimization reaches
 * ~0.89); it is the band on which THIS clean certificate certifies LARGE-SIGNAL
 * descent. (V>0 on the band: det P_full=(41-10d-39d^2)/48>0 for d<~0.90.)
 *
 * WHY NOT the full box [ODE]V<bound parametrically: the nonlinear dI at
 * symbolic d times out (QE in 5 vars d,w1,w2,s,c). This descent certificate is
 * the parametric large-signal core; the full sublevel-set invariance box is
 * machine-checked at the fixed instance (theorem_ph_bridge).
 */

ProgramVariables
  Real d; Real w1; Real w2; Real s;
End.

Problem
  \forall d \forall w1 \forall w2 \forall s (
    ( 0 < d & d <= 2/5 )
    ->
    (   /* 6 * V'|_{c=1} <= 0 */
        9*d^2*s*w2 + 3*d*s^2 + 2*d*s*w1 - 5*d*s*w2 + 6*d*w1^2 + 3*d*w1*w2
          + 3*d*w2^2 - 3*s^2 - 4*s*w1 - 2*s*w2 - 6*w1^2 - 3*w1*w2 - 3*w2^2 <= 0
      & /* 30 * V'|_{c=4/5} <= 0 */
        45*d^2*s*w2 + 15*d*s^2 + 2*d*s*w1 - 17*d*s*w2 + 24*d*w1^2 + 12*d*w1*w2
          + 24*d*w2^2 - 15*s^2 - 22*s*w1 - 8*s*w2 - 36*w1^2 - 12*w1*w2 - 12*w2^2 <= 0 ) )
End.

Tactic "Proof"
